WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:06.080
The Da Vinci Surgical System is the  
most advanced robot in surgery.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.600
It doesn't operate alone: it's a slave robot  
that follows every surgeon's movement,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:18.440
enhancing precision and eliminating  
hand tremors. The doctor sits at a console,

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:24.280
from where they control robotic arms  
and see inside the patient in 3D and HD,

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:29.320
as if they were inside the body.  
They can also view prior images,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:35.960
biopsies, and even use fluorescence  
to detect blood vessels and reduce bleeding.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:41.000
Among its advantages: less blood loss,  
fewer complications, shorter hospital stays,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.960
and a much faster recovery. In short,  
Da Vinci doesn't replace the surgeon…

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:54.200
it empowers them. It's the best example  
of how technology makes medicine more

00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:00.280
precise, safe, and human. A clear sign  
that robotics is transforming surgery.